  "observation": "Pinned applications now preserve workspace2, size108x440, pin state and the unsaved draft through the original first output removal, replacement, all-output disappearance and fresh return. Owning workspace migration avoids retired-owner gap callbacks and pinned stay-behind paths; the existing native authority permits explicit same-output navigation to the preserved workspace before pin focus. Actual taskbar Activate/Restore and native pointer/keyboard/draft/pixels pass for pinned and previously minimized applications. Real cross-output pin activation remains Refused without transfer; a live-monitor workspace move retains the pin on its old output. The prior pinned smaller/negative-origin journey passes the exact tuple with normal cleanup.",
  "missingObservations": [
    "Independent original UI-019 acceptance and physical hotplug/AT/IME remain open.",
    "Fullscreen/grouped/modal families, wider scale/rotation/output combinations, concurrent gestures/custody/protected input/Unknown and other native-host/transport schedules remain open. Oversized clients retain their original size; this does not prove whole-client fit.",
    "Post-first-unplug/pre-zero fixture setup exposed an Active/Minimize cue while pinning selected another active workspace; original taskbar-active focus/visibility/custody must be reproduced and reconciled separately. The final pin/min fixtures are established before the first unplug and validate the broader original journey.",
    "Full original hardware/resource/journey evidence, reproducible package and reversible deployment/rollback remain open."
  ],
  "sourceBoundary": "Retired/absent old monitor skips gap-navigation callbacks and pinned stay-behind. Live-owner workspace moves retain existing behavior. Native same-focus-output pin recovery uses the existing explicit owner-navigation path; cross-output implicit transfer stays refused. No new frontend policy or compensating effect.",
  "coreBoundary": {
    "changedSources": [
      "native/core/WorkspacePlacementController.cpp"
    ],
    "rebuiltArchiveMembers": {
      "WorkspacePlacementController.cpp.o": "fad1269635fafc459cced1eda08164552d2dd6f96ecbdd506b64bec5e6b26ea7"
    },
    "unchangedArchiveMembers": 432,
    "existingPublicHeadersUnchanged": true,
    "existingObjectLayoutsUnchanged": true,
    "existingStrongExportsPreserved": true,
    "plugin": "Changed owning authority TU rebuilt against this exact core; no missing strong symbols. Existing host/Elm/Aquamarine remain exact; actual native loads/actions qualified. No installation or main desktop activation."
  },
  "modelScope": "One compositor-thread owner with separate retirement, skipped retired gap callback, migration, all-output loss, return and admitted taskbar recovery. Legacy gap/ownership counterexample and same-output admission refusal retained. Final model includes native admission/navigation and cross-output refusal, live-owner pin behavior, positive witnesses and sampled safety. Coordinates, transport, modal/custody/fullscreen/hardware/AT and liveness are outside this model; original coordinate/native observations remain separate.",
  "probeDisposition": {
    "retainedFailures": [
      "model-reserved-name-failure",
      "native-before",
      "probe-admission-refusal",
      "probe-inactive-pin",
      "probe-late-pin-guard",
      "probe-private-focus-timeout",
      "probe-taskbar-inactive-pin"
    ],
    "corrections": "Pinning an inactive application intentionally attaches it to the active workspace. Late pin guard alone missed the earlier gap callback; fixed migration then exposed actual implicit-transfer-required refusal. Direct fixture activation timed out before removal, and taskbar setup after first unplug exposed an Active/Minimize/owner mismatch. Final fixture establishes state before the first removal and exercises both original removal stages with real taskbar activation/minimize where needed. No deadline extension or post-removal focus/geometry workaround. Model built-in parameter names were corrected before production implementation; later model refinements retain the missing callback/admission findings.",
    "scope": "Early narrower/provisional models and probes are retained as historical diagnostics, not proofs of final behavior."
  },
  "nativeFixtureScope": "Final pinned fixture uses supported native pin dispatch before the first output removal, preserving its then-active workspace. Minimized fixture uses the actual taskbar before that removal. Original popup/no-match/output-removal/zero-return/keyboard-read recovery is retained; returned taskbar actions and client input are real native interactions. Later guard fixtures use supported native monitor/workspace commands and one explicitly Refused native client activation; no claim of GUI refusal rendering from that direct guard call.",
  "reviewerDisposition": {
    "name": "root-pinned-output-retirement",
    "independent": false,
    "disposition": "Owner-observed protected native/compiled/sampled results; original independent acceptance remains open."
  }
